Header Value <code>X-Kiestoon-Event</code> the event name <code>X-Kiestoon-Delivery</code> unique id of this delivery <code>X-Kiestoon-Timestamp</code> Unix time in seconds <code>X-Kiestoon-Signature</code> <code>sha256=</code> + hex HMAC-SHA256 of <code>&lt;timestamp&gt;.&lt;body&gt;</code> with the webhook secret <p>Check the signature and reject old timestamps (for example older than 5 minutes):</p> <pre><code>import hmac, hashlib, time

def valid(secret: str, timestamp: str, body: bytes, signature: str) -&gt; bool:
    if abs(time.time() - int(timestamp)) &gt; 300:
        return False
    mac = hmac.new(secret.encode(), timestamp.encode() + b"." + body, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()
    return hmac.compare_digest("sha256=" + mac, signature)
</code></pre> <p>Answer with a 2xx status within 10 seconds. Other answers are retried after 10 seconds and after 1 minute. Redirects are not followed, and webhooks to this server itself (localhost) are refused; addresses in your own network are allowed. The last 200 deliveries of each webhook are shown in the portal.</p>

